    # Additional body templates
    "Annual performance reviews are conducted on a cycle established by the Human Resources Department and communicated to employees at the beginning of each review year. Employees are evaluated against pre-established goals, behavioral competencies, and organizational values. Results are shared with employees in a one-on-one meeting with their manager.",
    "The Company's leave programs are designed to support employees through significant life events while maintaining operational continuity. Employees are encouraged to plan leave in advance whenever possible and to communicate with their managers about anticipated absences.",
    "All employees are required to complete mandatory compliance training within 30 days of hire and annually thereafter. Training programs are administered through the Company's learning management system and completion is tracked by the Human Resources Department. Failure to complete mandatory training by the deadline may result in disciplinary action.",
    "{org_name} maintains an Employee Advisory Council consisting of non-management employees selected through a nomination process. The Council provides input to senior leadership on policy matters, workplace concerns, and organizational initiatives. Council membership does not constitute a waiver of any employment rights.",
    "The Company's progressive discipline process is designed to give employees a meaningful opportunity to correct performance or conduct issues before more serious action is taken. However, {org_name} reserves the right to skip steps in the process or proceed directly to termination when circumstances warrant.",
    "Employees who believe they have been subjected to discrimination, harassment, or retaliation have multiple reporting options: direct supervisor (unless the supervisor is the alleged wrongdoer), the Human Resources Department, any member of senior leadership, or the Company's anonymous ethics hotline at 1-800-555-0198.",
    "Background checks will be conducted on all candidates who receive a conditional offer of employment. The scope of the background check will vary by role and may include criminal history, employment verification, education verification, professional license verification, and credit history where permitted by applicable law.",
    "All Company-owned equipment — including laptops, mobile devices, access credentials, and physical keys or badges — must be returned within 24 hours of the last day of employment. Employees who fail to return equipment in good working condition may be responsible for replacement costs to the extent permitted by applicable law.",
    "The Company does not permit employees to accept gifts or benefits from vendors, clients, or other third parties that could create, or appear to create, a conflict of interest. Items of nominal value (not to exceed $25 retail) may be accepted where refusal would be culturally inappropriate or create business awkwardness.",
    "Employees who need workplace accommodations related to a disability, pregnancy, sincerely held religious belief, or other protected characteristic should contact the Human Resources Department to initiate the interactive accommodation process. The Company engages in good-faith dialogue with employees to identify effective accommodations.",
    "The Company uses electronic monitoring tools, including internet use logs, email scanning, and access-control records, to ensure compliance with its policies and protect organizational assets. Employees have no expectation of privacy with respect to activity on Company systems, networks, or premises.",
    "Drug and alcohol testing may be conducted at hire (for safety-sensitive positions), following a workplace accident or near-miss, when reasonable suspicion exists, and as part of a return-to-duty agreement. Testing is conducted by a certified third-party administrator using methods approved by the U.S. Department of Transportation where applicable.",
    "Employees who incur moving expenses as part of a Company-approved relocation should submit documented receipts to Human Resources within 60 days of the move. Reimbursements are subject to current IRS tax treatment requirements, and employees should consult their personal tax advisor regarding imputed income.",
